  <section class="section teal-soft">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="reveal">What the data buyer looks for</h2>
      <p class="reveal">The data buyer is looking for a specific type of company. As a starting point:</p>
      <ul class="checklist reveal">
        <li><strong>30+ full-time U.S. office staff</strong>10+ for accounting, finance or medical firms, 6+ for law firms.</li>
        <li><strong>3+ years of operating history</strong>With those years of records still in the company&rsquo;s systems.</li>
        <li><strong>At least five systems</strong>Email, internal chat, file storage, CRM, plus one more. Records spread across tools, not one archive.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="reveal">More than half the staff must be U.S.-based, and the company must own the records. Each deal is confirmed separately by the data buyer.</p>
    </div>
